  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Multisectoral Emergency Response to Conflict and Climate Shocks to Affected Populations in Northern Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With this grant, the International Organization for Migration continues to respond to crises arising from the ongoing conflict and recurrent disasters affecting Mozambique. Under this project, IOM provides humanitarian assistance through the deployment of an Integrated Multi-sectoral Settlements Approach in the districts identified as having a high concentration of multisectoral humanitarian needs, including of Quissanga, Macomia, Metuge and Mocimboa da Praia (Cabo Delgado province). Sectoral responses are being implemented in other districts with high sectoral-specific humanitarian needs in other locations, including Nangade, Ibo, Muidumbe, Pemba Districts (Cabo Delgado province) as well as other district/province across the country in case humanitarian needs arise.</narrative>
  </description>
